AUDIO: 'My name is Alden Peters and I created Friends of Sophia Tidbits and Bites. Friends of Sophia is a completely original IP about human tidbits and robot bites and their comedic relationship in an oppressive cyberpunk'

[00:20] [scene:production]
VISUAL: Alden Peters and an actor on a green screen set, with a tracking marker visible.
AUDIO: 'world. It\'s inspired by The Matrix, Bladeunner, The Fifth Element, and Star Trek. These are the kinds of sci-fi worlds that I always wanted to go live in and explore and inspired me to want to be a filmmaker. So, that\'s the kind'

[00:33] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A detailed shot of a cinema camera rig with an iPhone attached, presumably running Jetset.
AUDIO: 'of world I wanted to create. We did this with a crew of about six people and one actor in front of a green screen. And I was able to do it with an iPhone app called Jetet, which you put'

[00:45] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A 3D animation software UI, likely Blender, showing a character model and animation timeline.
AUDIO: 'on your camera and it captures the shot and all the tracking data and brings it right into a 3D program like Blender or Unreal Engine. It gave me the freedom to shoot on a green screen, even handheld, and not have to worry about any of the'

[00:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tracking data. So, I could do all the VFX myself without having to spend hundreds of thousands of dollars to create a world like this. Alternative tracking technologies are just prohibitively expensive. So, there is absolutely no way I could have done a'

